E cover in place as soon as possible, given the implications of any delay. &nbsp;Could we set up a call today to align and move things forward? &nbsp;Let me know what time works for you.&nbsp;Thanks,Helena&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Helena&nbsp;YearwoodRisk&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;Compliance&nbsp;DirectorFrom:&nbsp;James Burke &lt;james.burke2@wtwco.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;06 October 2025 18:30To:&nbsp;Sarah Bingham &lt;sbingham@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jonathan Simon &lt;Jonathan.Simon@wtwco.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jamie Macfarlane &lt;jmacfarlane@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;RE: Enquiry for Additional ATE Cover – Pan-NOx Emissions Litigation&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Hi Sarah/Anna,&nbsp;I hope that the PTR went well today.&nbsp;Following our enquiries about additional insurance, insurers have asked the following questions so that they can better advise as to whether they can offer cover:&nbsp;Full details of developments in the litigation since we last spoke to PG? There is no need to re-cover the issues raised with insurers prior to today’s PTR, all other developments however need advising.Full details of any further emissions department changes at PG since we last spoke?An update concerning recruitment into the department following the departures of Michael Burke, Pete Gallagher and if applicable, any others&nbsp;Insurers have also been asking numerous times for a technical call on NOx to be re-arranged since it was postponed from 2nd&nbsp;September. We have offered them Wednesday at 3pm but not all insurers are available at that time. Please can you provide a range of times that you would be available for the call?&nbsp;Kind regards,&nbsp;James Burke&nbsp;Associate Director (Solicitor)Litigation and Contingent Risk FINEX Global&nbsp;WTWOn behalf of Willis Limited, 51 Lime Street, London, EC3M 7DQ (registered number 181116)On behalf of Willis Towers Watson SA/NV, Quai des Vennes, 4020, Liège, Belgium (registered as a branch in the UK at 51 Lime Street, London, EC3M 7DQ UK Branch Number BR021056) in relation to all EEA-regulated business&nbsp;D: +44 (0)20 31248037M: +44 (0)7831 162591&nbsp;james.burke2@wtwco.comwww.wtwco.com&nbsp;Financial, Professional, and Executive Risks (FINEX)Your Trusted Partner in Managing Complex Risk: Expertly navigating Litigation Risk, Cyber, Directors &amp; Officers, Financial Institutions, Mergers &amp; Acquisitions, Professional Indemnity, and Operational Risks within WTW.Part of our wider risk solutions capabilities at WTW&nbsp;At WTW we work flexibly - whilst you may receive emails from me out of working hours, I do not expect a response or action outside your own working hours.&nbsp;&nbsp;From:&nbsp;Sarah Bingham &lt;sbingham@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;30 September 2025 18:14To:&nbsp;James Burke &lt;james.burke2@wtwco.com&gt;; Jonathan Simon &lt;Jonathan.Simon@wtwco.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jamie Macfarlane &lt;jmacfarlane@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Re: Enquiry for Additional ATE Cover – Pan-NOx Emissions Litigation&nbsp;Hi James,Thank you for your timely response.I do not yet have instructions on the date by which any top-up may need to be secured, as the Security for Costs hearing has not yet been listed.In the meantime, could you please approach the insurers and ask whether, in principle, the following top-ups could be feasible under the PG Wrapper?&nbsp;Mercedes&nbsp;-£953,580.35Ford-£838,961.27Renault-Nissan-£2,535,219.93PCD-£149,635.79Toyota-£136,927.40&nbsp;Many thanks,Sarah​​​​Sarah&nbsp;BinghamLegal&nbsp;Director+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7484&nbsp;085&nbsp;187This email a