Hey Donatas&nbsp;See latest comms on the Nox ATE topup&nbsp;James and Jonathan ar&nbsp;From: Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 30 October 2025 10:01To: James Burke &lt;James.Burke2@wtwco.com&gt;; Jonathan Simon &lt;Jonathan.Simon@wtwco.com&gt;Cc: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Enquiry for Additional ATE Cover – Pan-NOx Emissions Litigation&nbsp;Hi James,&nbsp;I’ve attached a note from Counsel that was provided a few weeks ago.&nbsp;I appreciate this may not align exactly with what we discussed, but could you consider whether it might be helpful given the circumstances?&nbsp;Kind regards &nbsp;Helena &nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Helena&nbsp;YearwoodRisk&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;Compliance&nbsp;DirectorFrom: James Burke &lt;James.Burke2@wtwco.com&gt; Sent: 29 October 2025 15:42To: Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jonathan Simon &lt;Jonathan.Simon@wtwco.com&gt;Cc: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Enquiry for Additional ATE Cover – Pan-NOx Emissions Litigation&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Thanks Helena.&nbsp;An update from Toremis – they have been going over the underwriting pack that we sent them. We included the original merits advice for the relevant matters, but to bring this up-to-date they have asked if they can receive a short email/advice from Counsel:Confirming, at a high level, that, with the benefit of having now reviewed the expert and factual evidence (and the detailed legal position taken by the defendants) the merits remain at least as good as the original assessments (including confirming what the relevant percentage assessment is for each of the defendants).Confirming the position on the merits in relation to: (1) whether each of the defendants' vehicl